--Description:
-- Earlier attempts failed because no explicit unemployment-rate column exists and
-- we referenced non-existent field names.  The ACS dataset *does* provide the raw
-- counts we need:
--   • employment_status_unemployed           – number of unemployed persons
--   • employment_status_in_labor_force       – total civilian labor force
-- The unemployment rate is therefore
--     unemployed ÷ labor_force × 100.
-- To prepare for later joins we also parse the 5-digit county FIPS codes from
-- `geo_id` (chars 10–14: 2-digit state + 3-digit county).  The query returns
-- 20 sample rows so we can verify the derived rate.
